      "claimId": "MLS-CLM-42CA0AF2EC7822C790EFE2D3",
      "sectionKey": "En pocas palabras",
      "summary": "Ничто is a Russian negative pronoun meaning ‘nothing’; the negative particle не is normally placed between a negative pronoun and the predicate.",
      "claimType": "general",
      "materiality": "substantial"
    },
    {
      "claimId": "MLS-CLM-18959175360932B018D84F22",
      "sectionKey": "Cómo funciona",
      "summary": "Ничто declines like что, with ничто in nominative, ничего in genitive/accusative, ничему in dative, ничем in instrumental, and ни о чём in a prepositional construction; the preposition is placed between ни and что.",
      "claimType": "general",
      "materiality": "substantial"
    },
    {
      "claimId": "MLS-CLM-4482169B4EEEF77296E80F83",
      "sectionKey": "Examples",
      "summary": "The cited examples illustrate the nominative, genitive/accusative and prepositional negative pronoun forms and negative concordance.",
      "claimType": "general",
      "materiality": "substantial"
    },
    {
      "claimId": "MLS-CLM-6BA739FF773E82F09AA434B2",
      "sectionKey": "Ничего y нечего",
      "summary": "The impersonal construction нечего + infinitive means there is nothing to do, unlike ничего не делать, and can take a dative experiencer.",
      "claimType": "general",
      "materiality": "substantial"
    }
  ],
